WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.370
In real life, few of us would ever root for
someone to die, but it's a completely different

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.120
story when we’re watching TV.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.750
Knowing it's all just pretend allows us to
feel pretty good when we watch the bad guys

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.959
get what's coming to them.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:16.950
Here are some moments we cheered at the screen
while seeing despicable characters bite the

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.950
dust.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.040
As you'd expect, there are massive spoilers
ahead.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.670
Steve Newlin - True Blood

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.150
Steve Newlin may have been a vampire, but
he acted like a weasel.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.539
Initially part of an anti-vampire crusade,
Newlin changes his tune after becoming a vampire

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:30.539
himself.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:34.470
He pulls a number of dirty tricks over the
show's first six seasons, but Newlin finally

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.980
gets his just desserts in the season six episode
"Life Matters," roasting to death in the sun

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.620
while screaming his professions of love for
fellow vampire Jason Stackhouse—all in front

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.239
of his adamantly anti-vampire ex-wife.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:47.690
Fangs for nothing, Steve.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.190
George Foyet - Criminal Minds

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.370
Criminal Minds plumbed into some pretty dark
depths with the story of George Foyet, a.k.a.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.059
the Boston Reaper.

00:00:56.059 --> 00:01:00.949
This psycho cut a bloody swath of destruction
for years, tormenting the cops on his trail,

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:05.030
until the case comes to a tragic conclusion
in the show's fifth season.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.590
During Criminal Minds' 100th episode, FBI
agent Aaron "Hotch" Hotchner finally catches

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.479
Foyet—but only after he murders Hotch's
wife.

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:18.649
In a blind rage, Hotch beats Foyet to death
with his bare hands, leaving millions of stunned

00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:22.189
viewers wishing they tuned into a rerun of
Dharma and Greg instead.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:24.939
Viserys Targaryen - Game of Thrones

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:26.329
If you've ever read George R.R.

00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:30.770
Martin's bestselling series, you know there’s
a lot going on, and it would take far too

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.329
much space to detail the royal intrigue leading
up to Viserys Targaryen's death in Game of

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:36.329
Thrones.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:40.420
Suffice it to say that aside from being the
exiled son of an assassinated king, Viserys

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.179
is also a pretty magnificent jerk.

00:01:43.179 --> 00:01:46.679
Even though it was still only the first season
of the show when he drunkenly challenged his

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:52.070
only real ally, the horselord Khal Drogo,
he'd already earned more than enough bad-guy

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:56.560
points to deserve death by molten metal crown,
fit for a king-sized tool.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.499
Of course, Viserys isn’t the only person
in Game of Thrones with a death wish...

00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:03.499
Joffrey Baratheon - Game of Thrones

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:08.610
In a way, it's hard to blame Joffrey Baratheon
for being such a sniveling little creep.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.231
After all, he was the product of inbreeding,
and growing up in a royal court meant he was

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:13.550
constantly spoiled.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:19.030
Still, that doesn't excuse his bloodthirsty
rule as king, or his violence against women.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.040
Committed to getting his own way at all costs,
Joffrey proved a consistent irritant during

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.340
Game of Thrones' first four seasons, so it
came as a delightful relief when he was poisoned

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.780
by his own grandmother-in-law at his wedding.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.480
Of all the many, many deaths Game of Thrones
has given viewers, Joffrey's extermination

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.830
has to be the most satisfying.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.730
Robert Romano - ER

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.350
Unlike most of the characters on this list,
ER's Robert Romano wasn't a killer, or even

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.760
a criminal—he was just the token smug doctor
that every hospital show has to have.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.450
It's to actor Paul McCrane's credit that Romano
ended up being such a satisfying, love-to-hate-'em

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.040
thorn in the staff's side.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.180
After being introduced in the show's fourth
season, he manages to offend, alienate, and

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.070
insult just about every other character, all
while adding to the top-rated show's consistently

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.200
riveting drama.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.020
Romano goes out with a bang in Season 10,
paying for his TV sins by being crushed under

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.470
a helicopter that falls off the hospital roof.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.730
At that point, we were more worried about
the helicopter.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.700
Philip Blake - The Walking Dead

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.840
Like any good sociopath, The Walking Dead's
Governor, Philip Blake, is enough of a smooth

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.880
talker to keep his true nature hidden from
his friends and allies, for a short time at

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.880
least.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.460
During the show's third and fourth seasons,
Blake's bloodlust and thirst for power are

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.910
revealed in small increments.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:35.060
By the time we figure out he's a murderous
lunatic who keeps his own zombified daughter

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.960
restrained in his apartment, we're pretty
much counting down the days until his death.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:43.581
Even for The Walking Dead, the Governor's
demise is pretty gruesome, but if viewers

00:03:43.581 --> 00:03:47.610
ever wanted to see anyone get stabbed in the
back, shot in the head, and left in a field

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.910
to be dismembered, it was ol’ One Eye.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.350
Speaking of putting your eye out…

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.880
Gustavo Fring - Breaking Bad

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.450
If you start selling meth for a living, you're
bound to run into some pretty unsavory characters.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:03.780
Case in point: Gus Fring, the powerful, lethal
dealer who starts tightening a noose around

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.060
Walter White’s neck almost immediately after
he reaches out to him about distributing his

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.210
perfect product.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.890
Throughout the show's third and fourth seasons,
Gus and Walter fight each other for the upper

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:18.420
hand in their relationship, with enough twists,
turns, and double-crosses for an entire series.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:23.740
We felt a powerful rush of satisfaction when
Walter finally got rid of Gus by booby-trapping

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.770
an enemy's wheelchair with a bomb that took
off half of Gus’s face… and a small chunk

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:29.990
of a nursing home.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:31.030
Real nice, Walt.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.080
Arthur Mitchell - Dexter

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.340
John Lithgow went from playing 3rd Rock from
the Sun's doofy sitcom dad to giving us the

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:42.760
creeps as Arthur Mitchell, the spine-tingling
serial murderer known as the "Trinity Killer"

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.330
in the fourth season of Dexter.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.870
Lithgow's soft-spoken demeanor made him the
perfect choice to play a guy whose near-perfect

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:52.460
suburban existence masks a terrifying urge
to kill.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:56.710
This helped fill the entire season with a
steadily mounting sense of dread that still

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.410
lingered even after Dexter manages to finally
put an end to Mitchell's murderous ways.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.580
In a sickening twist, the show undercut the
viewer's relief over the Trinity Killer's

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:10.200
death by revealing that Dexter caught Mitchell
too late to prevent him from committing his

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.640
last murder: Dexter's own wife, Rita.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.920
Ralph Cifaretto - The Sopranos

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:20.040
A career criminal whose tendency toward violent
outbursts was overlooked because of his ability

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:24.060
to get things done, Ralphie was a longtime
burr in Tony's saddle.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.940
If Sopranos fans hated Ralph after he murdered
a stripper in the parking lot of the gang's

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.440
favorite club, they really couldn't stand
him after he started a stable fire that killed

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.730
a horse he owned with Tony.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:38.639
It was the last straw for Tony, who offed
Ralphie with his own bare hands and disposed

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:39.680
of the body in pieces.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.910
And as Viserys Targaryen taught us, you don't
want to mess with a dude and his horses.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.230
Thanks for watching!

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:49.150
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.250
And leave us a comment to let us know which
TV death you thought was the most satisfying...

